# Build context for Dockerfile.gates ONLY. BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over
# `.dockerignore`, which is the whole point: the gate image needs `tests/` and `alembic/`, and
# the shipped image must keep excluding them.
#
# DO NOT collapse the env lines into `.env.*`. That glob also eats `.env.example` and
# `.env.test.example`, which are TRACKED SAMPLE files the config suite parses — five tests in
# tests/test_config.py go red, and the failure looks like a rebase regression rather than a
# context problem. Real secrets are excluded by name; live values are passed at `docker run`.
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.ty_cache
.env
.env.bak-*
.env.production.local
.env.worker*
.env.e2e-*
.env.test
docker-compose*.yml
